 ## Qualification follow-up — 2026-10-28
 
 The qualification worktree implements persisted review context counts, with zero for new empty lists and unknown for older records; its live review exported 2. Two separately authorized S05 design trials on 2.2.0 were rejected and recorded without retroactive D3 allowance debit. Candidate 65dbafd0 (2.2.1) passed Node 20 release checks, offline packaging, side-by-side installation, matched preparation and native readiness. Both qualification starts are consumed: review accepted independently; edit arithmetic and tests pass but its equivalent strict assertion import fails the unchanged literal contract, so it is closed rejected. The nested probe was unavailable; no sidecar permission follows. Evidence is linked from Handoff and the per-build ledger. No publication, extra start or integration follows these results.
+
+## Validation and acceptance repair — 2026-10-28
+
+Repeated boundary trials exposed two coordinator-workflow defects: an unnecessary literal strict-assert import check rejected equivalent code, and copy-only validation still required dependency-installation metadata. The local usability follow-up removes that incidental literal from future example contracts, requires criterion provenance and baseline preflight, and separates named test-framework inspection from behavioral checks. Copy-only preparation must reconstruct generic Git fixtures without invoking a package manager; dependency installation keeps the reviewed offline profile. Original frozen-contract failures and exact patches remain unchanged. This is a local source repair; installed/archive qualification and publication remain separate. See [the EDD follow-up](vibe-usability-edd-20261028.md#follow-up-amendment-4--reported-integration-test-failures).
+
+## Mechanism resilience review — 2026-10-28
